{"name":"Sakura Mochi","hex":"#cea19f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sakura","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Japanese) cherry tree","cherry blossom (blossom of the Japanese cherry tree)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sakura"},{"term":"mochi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small Japanese rice cake made from glutinous rice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mochi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sakuramochi","blocks":[{"text":"Sakuramochi  is a Japanese confection (wagashi) consisting of sweet, pink-colored rice cake (mochi) with red bean paste (anko) filling, wrapped in a pickled cherry blossom (sakura) leaf, which may or may not be eaten depending on individual preference."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/A_rice_cake_filled_with_sweet_bean_paste_and_wrapped_in_a_pickled_cherry_leaf%2Ckatori-city%2Cjapan.JPG/330px-A_rice_cake_filled_with_sweet_bean_paste_and_wrapped_in_a_pickled_cherry_leaf%2Ckatori-city%2Cjapan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sakuramochi","wikidata":"Q1087577"},{"title":"Cherry blossom","blocks":[{"text":"The cherry blossom, or sakura, is the flower of trees in Prunus subgenus Cerasus. Sakura usually refers to flowers of ornamental cherry trees, such as cultivars of Prunus serrulata, not trees grown for their fruit. Cherry blossoms have been described as having a vanilla-like smell, which is mainly attributed to coumarin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg/330px-Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_blossom","wikidata":"Q871991"},{"title":"Mochi","blocks":[{"text":"Mochi is a Japanese rice cake made of mochigome (もち米), a short-grain japonica glutinous rice, and sometimes other ingredients such as water, sugar, and cornstarch. The steamed rice is pounded into paste and molded into the desired shape. In Japan, it is traditionally made in a ceremony called mochitsuki . While eaten year-round, mochi is a traditional food for the Japanese New Year, and is commonly sold and eaten during that time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Mochi_002.jpg/330px-Mochi_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mochi","wikidata":"Q470519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Sakuramochi.jpg/500px-Sakuramochi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Sakuramochi.jpg/500px-Sakuramochi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kansai-style sakuramochi","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASakuramochi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Sakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg/500px-Sakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Sakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg/1280px-Sakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Sakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg/500px-Sakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The interior of a sakuramochi, showing the red-bean paste inside","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASakuramochi%2C_inside.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.